  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refugee Support, Empowerment and Transformation (Re-SET)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme is targeting to provide refugee support in Uganda that is beyond an emergency framing onto a longer-term more sustainable footing. This will be delivered through three pillars below.
 Acute humanitarian needs will be provided but to the most highly vulnerable based upon an up-to-date needs assessment. 
Self-Reliance and Resilience will be prioritised, supporting refugees and host communities to transition from poverty and vulnerability by building livelihoods and income generating opportunities using market-led approaches and private sector linkages
System Change targeting impactful areas of transformation.  This could include technical support for the transition of services, Refugee Engagement Forums, and establishment of a data and learning facility</narrative>
  </description>
